      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two series of styrylcarbonyl 3-phenylsydnone derivatives, 4-[1-oxo-(3-substituted aryl)-2-propenyl]-3-phenylsydnones (series 1, 1-21) and 3-[4-[3-(substituted aryl)-1-oxo-2-propenyl]phenyl]sydnones (series II, 22-40), were synthesized and evaluated pharmacologically at a dose of 100 mg/kg po. Eleven compounds in series I plus one in series II and six in series I plus seven in series II were active in the carrageenan-induced edema and acetic acid-induced writhing assays, respectively. Compound 35 in the latter assay showed activity somewhat similar to that of the positive control drug, aspirin, administered at the same dosage. Compounds 11, 17, and 23 showed activity in both assays, and 23 also was active in the adjuvant-induced arthritis assay."},
